# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development environment
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local dev does NOT need any production secrets. The local Next.js server
# routes all database, Cloudflare R2, and email operations through the
# production Genggi API (https://genggi.com by default), which holds the real
# MONGODB_URI / R2_* / RESEND_API_KEY / AUTH_SECRET.
#
#   Local Next.js  ->  Genggi production API  ->  Production Database / R2
#
# The only value a contributor needs locally is the shared dev token below.

# Shared bearer token that authenticates the local dev server to the
# production Genggi API's internal routes (/api/internal/*). Set the SAME
# value on the production deployment (GENGGI_API_TOKEN) and give it to each
# contributor. It grants privileged access — keep it server-side only and
# NEVER prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
GENGGI_API_TOKEN=

# Optional: override the production API base URL (defaults to https://genggi.com).
# GENGGI_API_URL=https://genggi.com

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production-only (DO NOT set for local dev)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are read only by the production deployment. They are listed here for
# reference so operators know what the Genggi API server needs configured. Do
# NOT put them in your local .env.local — local dev must work without them.
#
# AUTH_SECRET=
# MONGODB_URI=
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# RESEND_FROM=
# R2_BUCKET=
# R2_ENDPOINT=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_PUBLIC_URL=
